  nesnd_usm_luo_last: "Luo"
  nesnd_civic_characters.16.t: "Accounts and Women Workers’ Literacy"
- nesnd_civic_characters.16.d: "Luo Yingtang organises literacy through workshop accounts and women workers’ mutual aid. Her public work raises questions of educational standing, but a government endorsement does not itself grant a state office or a delegate’s qualification."
- nesnd_civic_characters.16.a: "Endorse the public proposal."
- nesnd_civic_characters.16.b: "Let the public debate continue."
- nesnd_civic_characters.116.t: "Accounts and Women Workers’ Literacy: The Debate Continues"
- nesnd_civic_characters.116.d: "The questions raised by Yingtang Luo have entered local organisations and public business. The advocate can still participate, while practical decisions depend on actual budgets, schools and industry."
- nesnd_civic_characters.116.organisation: "The original advocate is no longer active in public life here. Local organisations and people in workshops and schools continue the dispute. A departure does not itself resolve the question."
- nesnd_civic_characters.116.a: "The work must continue."
+ nesnd_civic_characters.16.d: "Luo Yingtang approaches literacy through workshop accounts and women workers’ mutual aid. Workers who can read an account can question wages and debts. Their demand for learning reaches from the work sheds towards the academies, bringing educational qualifications into public debate."
+ nesnd_civic_characters.16.a: "Endorse women workers’ access to literacy."
+ nesnd_civic_characters.16.b: "Let the case for mutual aid and education spread."
+ nesnd_civic_characters.116.t: "Qualifications After Literacy"
+ nesnd_civic_characters.116.d: "Luo Yingtang continues to approach education through accounts and women workers’ mutual aid. Reading wage accounts and invoices gives workers grounds to speak for themselves. Whether that learning can win public recognition becomes a question of their own."
+ nesnd_civic_characters.116.organisation: "Luo Yingtang is no longer active in public life here. Women workers still seek literacy through mutual aid, bringing the prospects opened by that learning before schools and the existing system of qualifications."
+ nesnd_civic_characters.116.a: "Let the learners state their needs."
  nesnd_usm_han_first: "Shiduo"
  nesnd_usm_han_last: "Han"
  nesnd_civic_characters.17.t: "The Craftsmen’s School"
- nesnd_civic_characters.17.d: "Han Shiduo connects technical learning with wages, injuries and hiring disputes. Even where workers’ organisations are weak, he can speak; that does not make him the representative of every worker in the country."
- nesnd_civic_characters.17.a: "Endorse the public proposal."
- nesnd_civic_characters.17.b: "Let the public debate continue."
- nesnd_civic_characters.117.t: "The Craftsmen’s School: The Debate Continues"
- nesnd_civic_characters.117.d: "The questions raised by Shiduo Han have entered local organisations and public business. The advocate can still participate, while practical decisions depend on actual budgets, schools and industry."
- nesnd_civic_characters.117.organisation: "The original advocate is no longer active in public life here. Local organisations and people in workshops and schools continue the dispute. A departure does not itself resolve the question."
- nesnd_civic_characters.117.a: "The work must continue."
+ nesnd_civic_characters.17.d: "Han Shiduo calls for technical education for craftsmen, connecting schools with disputes over wages, injuries and hiring. Manufacturers need skilled hands and workers rely on their skills for a living. Who should pay for training concerns them both."
+ nesnd_civic_characters.17.a: "Endorse the craftsmen’s case for skills and livelihoods."
+ nesnd_civic_characters.17.b: "Let craftsmen state their own demands."
+ nesnd_civic_characters.117.t: "Skill and Livelihood"
+ nesnd_civic_characters.117.d: "Han Shiduo continues to connect craftsmen’s schools with wages and injuries. Workshops need skilled hands; craftsmen want to know whether training will improve their livelihoods. Technical education has entered the dispute between labour and employers."
+ nesnd_civic_characters.117.organisation: "Han Shiduo no longer participates in public life here. Craftsmen’s demands for learning and livelihoods still circulate among workshops: what is taught, who pays for it and what wages trained hands can command remain local questions."
+ nesnd_civic_characters.117.a: "Let training lead towards a livelihood."
  nesnd_usm_jiang_first: "Shaoheng"
